# The symbols of soft-linked frameworks that WebCore's Swift uses, one per line:
#     <function|constant|class> <framework> <symbol>
#     constant <framework> <symbol> as <type>      (an NSString constant of a typed string enum)
#     class <framework> <symbol> as <type>         (a class that the SDK renames in Swift)
#     member <framework> <class> <selector> <declaration>
#                                                  (an Objective-C member whose SDK declaration names a class of the
#                                                  framework: the Swift declaration, with NSArray and NSDictionary for its
#                                                  typed collections, and `[T] counted by <property>` for a `const T *`)
#     function <framework> <symbol> with pointer    (also the function's pointer, for real-time code to copy on the main thread)
# PAL must soft-link each one (pal/cf/AudioToolboxSoftLink.h, pal/cocoa/AVFoundationSoftLink.h, ...).
# Scripts/generate-soft-link-accessors.py generates the accessors, <framework>SoftLinkAccessors.swift, from this list.
# List only what Swift calls, so that the accessors stay small enough to review.

